 r←Test_Server_014(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;request;response;ind
⍝ Requests "robots.txt" and checks that it points to the sitemap and disallows nothing.
⍝ A disallowed page cannot be fetched, so its "noindex" is never seen and, when something
⍝ links to it, it can be indexed by its URL alone. Hence no path may be disallowed here.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 request←R.NewRequest 0
 request.RequestTarget←'/robots.txt'
 response←TC.SendAndReceive(TC.ReplaceRegistryAlias'[localhost]')request
 →T.PassesIf 200=response.StatusCode
 →T.PassesIf(≢response.Headers)≥ind←(⊃¨response.Headers)⍳⊂'content-type'
 →T.PassesIf∨/'text/plain'⍷ind 2⊃response.Headers
 →T.PassesIf∨/'User-agent: *'⍷response.Content
 →T.PassesIf∨/'Sitemap: https://'⍷response.Content
 →T.PassesIf∨/'/sitemap.xml'⍷response.Content
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'Disallow: /v1/tags'⍷response.Content
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'Disallow: /v1/credential-report'⍷response.Content
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'Disallow: /v1/version-information'⍷response.Content

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
